[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. define an influence line and tell it apart from a shear-force or bending-moment diagram;
2. derive the influence lines of the reactions and hinge forces of the model by statics alone;
3. sketch and check an influence line with the Müller–Breslau principle;
4. use an influence line for a single load, a pair of loads and a distributed load, and find the critical position;
5. reduce your gauge readings, compare them with theory and explain the differences.
